# netbird-sync gotchas

- A Hecate user's NetBird `id` is Dex's base64 protobuf: field 1 = Authentik
  `sub`, field 2 = connector id. Decode with varint lengths; accept url-safe
  and unpadded variants. A user whose id doesn't decode isn't a Hecate user.
- Only `issued: "jwt"` NetBird groups are managed — they're created by
  sign-in sync, never by this job. `api`-issued groups on a user are always
  preserved; claim names with no group are reported, never created.
- The `groups` claim is fetched through Authentik's property-mapping test
  endpoint (`POST /propertymappings/all/{pk}/test/`), which evaluates the
  mapping exactly as sign-in does. Don't reconstruct claims from group
  membership — they can drift.
- Alert state lives in a job-created ConfigMap (`netbird-sync-state`),
  deliberately not in Git: ArgoCD selfHeal would revert it. The Job's Role
  can only touch ConfigMaps in its own namespace.
- The Authentik service account is a separate blueprint ConfigMap
  (`authentik-blueprint-netbird-sync`) so a missing
  `NETBIRD_SYNC_AUTHENTIK_TOKEN` env can't fail the NetBird login blueprint.
- The NetBird PAT expires in 365 days (max the API allows); expiry shows up
  as the failure email, then rotate per the README.
- No package.json reaches the pod (ConfigMap mount), so keep the TS
  CJS-safe: no top-level await; Node's module detection handles the imports.
